`org.apache.kafka.tools` is a good package. However, it is used by tool =
module already. Not sure whether it is good idea to use same package in =
different module. Maybe it is fine since we don=E2=80=99t expect user =
has to import both tool jar and client jar for developing plugins.

> 3. Also, should we follow the `storage-api` example and have a module =
for
> all extensible interfaces used by tools?

That seems good to me. However, it is a bit overkill if only few =
pluggable interfaces comes from tools. The rule I followed is =
server-side plugins (for example, AlterConfigPolicy, Authorizer, =
CreateTopicPolicy, and so on.

In short, I considered `org.apache.kafka.tools` before, but it is used =
by tool module already. If different modules has same package does not =
store up trouble for the future, I prefer the package =
``org.apache.kafka.tools``

